From: Ruslan Shevchenko <rshevchenko@neoflex.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dp: prefer DSC over driving eDP below 8 bpc

intel_dp_compute_link_config_wide() may reduce pipe_bpp all the way to
6 bpc for RGB to make a mode fit the link, and compression is only
considered after that search fails. On a panel that supports DSC the
result can be a link that is nowhere near saturated carrying a picture
with two bits per colour thrown away.

A concrete one: the eDP panel in a HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 (ZQC-P) is
3120x2080 at 120 Hz, declares 10 bpc in its EDID, and its DPCD offers
exactly two link rates, 2.7 and 5.4 Gbps. Four lanes of HBR2 leave
2160000 of headroom, 24 bpp needs 2702592 and 18 bpp needs 2026944, so
the driver settles on 18 bpp with dithering:

  DP link limits: pixel clock 900864 kHz DSC off max lanes 4
      max rate 540000 max pipe_bpp 30 min link_bpp 18.0000 max link_bpp 30.0000
  DP lane count 4 clock 540000 bpp input 18 compressed 0.0000
      link rate required 2026944 available 2160000
  hw max bpp: 30, pipe bpp: 18, dithering: 1

There is no "Try DSC" line anywhere in that log. The panel advertises
DSC 1.2 with 4 slices and 8 and 10 bpc decode, the VBT does not set
edp_dsc_disable for it, and forcing compression through debugfs gives
10 bpc with no dithering at less than half the link load:

  DP DSC computed with Input Bpp = 30 Compressed Bpp = 8.0000 Slice Count = 4
  DP lane count 4 clock 540000 bpp input 30 compressed 8.0000
      link rate required 900864 available 2160000

with a clean link: CR, EQ and symbol lock on all four lanes,
INTERLANE_ALIGN_DONE, and zero symbol errors.

Dithering down to 6 bpc predates DSC and was the right answer when the
alternative was no picture at all. Where the sink can decompress, it no
longer is. So when the uncompressed pass lands below 8 bpc on eDP while
the panel itself would take more, try compression instead.

This is a preference rather than a requirement, so it must never turn a
mode that works today into a rejected one: if the DSC pass fails for any
reason the uncompressed result is put back and the modeset proceeds as
before. It is deliberately limited to eDP, where the link is a fixed
property of the machine; on external DP a link that cannot carry 8 bpc
is more often a cable than a design.

One detail is easy to get wrong and is worth spelling out.
intel_dp_compute_config_limits() derives the DSC input depth from the pipe
bpp already in the crtc state:

  limits->pipe.max_bpp = clamp(crtc_state->pipe_bpp,
			       limits->pipe.min_bpp, limits->pipe.max_bpp);

When compression is required that is still the depth the modeset arrived
with. When it is merely preferred, the uncompressed search has already
written its own answer there, so feeding it back in compresses the reduced
depth rather than the one the panel can take: 18 clamps up to the DSC
minimum of 24 and stops, on a panel that would have taken 30. Measured on
the machine above, where the difference is 8 bits per colour against 10.
So the baseline is restored before the DSC pass.

Signed-off-by: Ruslan Shevchenko <rshevchenko@neoflex.ru>
Local adaptation for Omarchy 7.2.5-3: restore the complete DSC state and
FEC flag on preferred-DSC failure. intel_dp_dsc_reset_config() alone does
not clear compression_enabled_on_link after a late dotclock rejection.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
@@ -2936,7 +2936,11 @@
 		&pipe_config->hw.adjusted_mode;
 	struct intel_dp *intel_dp = enc_to_intel_dp(encoder);
 	struct link_config_limits limits;
-	bool dsc_needed, joiner_needs_dsc;
+	bool dsc_needed, joiner_needs_dsc, dsc_preferred = false;
+	int uncompressed_bpp = 0, uncompressed_clock = 0, uncompressed_lanes = 0;
+	typeof(pipe_config->dsc) uncompressed_dsc = {};
+	bool uncompressed_fec_enable = false;
+	int entry_bpp = pipe_config->pipe_bpp;
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	intel_dp_dsc_reset_config(pipe_config);
@@ -2971,6 +2975,33 @@
 					   0,
 					   num_joined_pipes))
 			dsc_needed = true;
+		else if (intel_dp_is_edp(intel_dp) &&
+			 pipe_config->pipe_bpp < 8 * 3 &&
+			 pipe_config->pipe_bpp < limits.pipe.max_bpp &&
+			 intel_dp_supports_dsc(intel_dp, connector, pipe_config)) {
+			/*
+			 * The uncompressed search is allowed to give up colour
+			 * depth to make a mode fit, down to 6 bpc for RGB. That
+			 * predates DSC, and where the sink can decompress it is
+			 * the worse of the two answers: an eDP panel driven at
+			 * 6 bpc with dithering has visibly less to work with
+			 * than the same panel at 8 bpc or better over a
+			 * compressed link.
+			 *
+			 * So when the link forced the pipe below 8 bpc while
+			 * the panel itself would take more, try compression
+			 * instead. This is a preference and not a requirement,
+			 * and it is deliberately not applied to external DP,
+			 * where a link that cannot carry 8 bpc is far more
+			 * often a cable than a design.
+			 */
+			uncompressed_dsc = pipe_config->dsc;
+			uncompressed_fec_enable = pipe_config->fec_enable;
+			uncompressed_bpp = pipe_config->pipe_bpp;
+			uncompressed_clock = pipe_config->port_clock;
+			uncompressed_lanes = pipe_config->lane_count;
+			dsc_preferred = true;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (dsc_needed && !intel_dp_supports_dsc(intel_dp, connector, pipe_config)) {
@@ -2978,33 +3009,80 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (dsc_needed) {
+	if (dsc_needed || dsc_preferred) {
 		int dsc_slice_count;
 
 		drm_dbg_kms(display->drm,
-			    "Try DSC (fallback=%s, joiner=%s, force=%s)\n",
+			    "Try DSC (fallback=%s, joiner=%s, force=%s, preferred=%s)\n",
 			    str_yes_no(ret), str_yes_no(joiner_needs_dsc),
-			    str_yes_no(intel_dp->force_dsc_en));
-
-		if (!intel_dp_compute_config_limits(intel_dp, conn_state, pipe_config,
-						    respect_downstream_limits,
-						    true,
-						    &limits))
-			return -EINVAL;
-
-		ret = intel_dp_dsc_compute_config(intel_dp, pipe_config,
-						  conn_state, &limits, 64);
-		if (ret < 0)
-			return ret;
-
-		dsc_slice_count = intel_dsc_line_slice_count(&pipe_config->dsc.slice_config);
-
-		if (!intel_dp_dotclk_valid(display,
-					   adjusted_mode->crtc_clock,
-					   adjusted_mode->crtc_htotal,
-					   dsc_slice_count,
-					   num_joined_pipes))
-			return -EINVAL;
+			    str_yes_no(intel_dp->force_dsc_en),
+			    str_yes_no(dsc_preferred));
+
+		ret = -EINVAL;
+
+		/*
+		 * intel_dp_compute_config_limits() derives the DSC input depth
+		 * from crtc_state->pipe_bpp:
+		 *
+		 *   limits->pipe.max_bpp = clamp(crtc_state->pipe_bpp,
+		 *				limits->pipe.min_bpp,
+		 *				limits->pipe.max_bpp);
+		 *
+		 * When DSC is required that value is still the one the modeset
+		 * arrived with. When it is merely preferred, the uncompressed
+		 * search has already written its own answer there, and feeding
+		 * that back in would compress the reduced depth instead of the
+		 * one the panel can actually take: 6 bpc clamps up to the DSC
+		 * minimum of 8 and stops, on a panel that would have taken 10.
+		 * Put the baseline back first.
+		 */
+		if (dsc_preferred)
+			pipe_config->pipe_bpp = entry_bpp;
+
+		if (intel_dp_compute_config_limits(intel_dp, conn_state, pipe_config,
+						   respect_downstream_limits,
+						   true,
+						   &limits)) {
+			ret = intel_dp_dsc_compute_config(intel_dp, pipe_config,
+							  conn_state, &limits, 64);
+
+			if (ret >= 0) {
+				dsc_slice_count =
+					intel_dsc_line_slice_count(&pipe_config->dsc.slice_config);
+
+				if (!intel_dp_dotclk_valid(display,
+							   adjusted_mode->crtc_clock,
+							   adjusted_mode->crtc_htotal,
+							   dsc_slice_count,
+							   num_joined_pipes))
+					ret = -EINVAL;
+			}
+		}
+
+		if (ret < 0) {
+			/*
+			 * Compression was required, so there is nothing to fall
+			 * back to and the mode genuinely cannot be driven.
+			 */
+			if (dsc_needed)
+				return ret;
+
+			/*
+			 * Compression was only preferred. Put back what the
+			 * uncompressed pass had already found: a dithered
+			 * picture beats a rejected modeset.
+			 */
+			drm_dbg_kms(display->drm,
+				    "DSC preferred but not usable, keeping %d bpp uncompressed\n",
+				    uncompressed_bpp);
+
+			/* Also restore compression_enabled_on_link after a late failure. */
+			pipe_config->dsc = uncompressed_dsc;
+			pipe_config->fec_enable = uncompressed_fec_enable;
+			pipe_config->pipe_bpp = uncompressed_bpp;
+			pipe_config->port_clock = uncompressed_clock;
+			pipe_config->lane_count = uncompressed_lanes;
+		}
 	}
 
 	drm_dbg_kms(display->drm,
